{"id":"kungsleden-north","title":"Kungsleden: Abisko to Nikkaluokta","who":"Classic route · Sweden's King's Trail through Lapland","when":"Late June to mid-September (midnight sun until late July)","vehicle":"On foot, 5–7 days, mountain huts","kind":"walk","color":"#0369a1","summary":"The northern classic of Sweden's long trail: from Abisko through birch forest and wide treeless valleys to the Tjäktja pass, then down to the Kebnekaise mountain station with a climb of Sweden's highest peak. Reindeer, Sami lands and STF huts with saunas; snow can linger on the pass into July.","sources":[{"label":"C. Sprague: Kungsleden, a little too fast (July 2025)","url":"https://cisprague.github.io/thoughts/kungsleden-2025.html"},{"label":"Swedish Tourist Association: Abisko–Nikkaluokta","url":"https://www.swedishtouristassociation.com/trails/abisko-nikkaluokta/"}],"approximate":"The usual huts; the line follows the trail where it was found.","km":99,"bbox":[18.3006,67.8359,19.0157,68.3502],"stops":[{"name":"Abisko","place":"Abisko Turiststation","at":[68.3502,18.83],"text":"The start, by the train station and Lake Torneträsk.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Lapporten_2.jpg/500px-Lapporten_2.jpg","page":"Abisko National Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lapporten_2.jpg","credit":"Lapplaender","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0 de"}},{"name":"Abiskojaure","place":"Abiskojaure","at":[68.2853,18.5797],"text":"Birch forest along the Abiskojåkka river to the first hut.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Lapporten_2.jpg/500px-Lapporten_2.jpg","page":"Abisko National Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lapporten_2.jpg","credit":"Lapplaender","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0 de"}},{"name":"Alesjaure","place":"Alesjaure","at":[68.1386,18.4186],"text":"Wide open valley, a Sami summer village and a hut with a sauna."},{"name":"Tjäktja Pass","place":"Tjäktja","at":[67.9831,18.3636],"text":